# Pi-hole wildcard denies - imported by `make import-wildcards`
#
# Gravity matches exact domains only, so a list entry for `example.com` does
# not cover `tracker.example.com`. Every parent below was already denied by an
# exact gravity entry while live subdomains of it resolved and connected; the
# wildcard closes that gap for the whole label.
#
# One domain per line, no `*.` prefix - `pihole --wild` adds the anchoring and
# stores it as regex `(\.|^)domain$`.
#
# Pure ad / attribution / telemetry: no user-visible function depends on these.
inmobi.com
amazon-adsystem.com
minerva.devices.a2z.com
mparticle.com
appsflyer.com
appsflyersdk.com
device.marketingcloudapis.com

# Deliberately NOT wildcarded (decided 2026-10-28). Each has leaking
# subdomains under an exact-denied parent, but the wildcard breaks real
# function, so the leak is accepted:
#   awstrack.me, klclick.com, klclick1.com  - SES/Klaviyo click redirectors;
#     wildcarding dead-ends links clicked inside emails
#   forter.com, signifyd.com                - checkout anti-fraud; can cause
#     purchases to fail on sites that gate on them
#   sentry.io                               - would also blackhole Sentry for
#     our own projects
